From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:29:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Evaluate a sequence key path into an Array

https://w3c.github.io/IndexedDB/#evaluate-a-key-path-on-a-value step 1.1 collects the values of a
sequence key path's items in "a new Array object created as if by the expression []", which then
converts to an array key. evaluate_key_path_on_value made an ordinary object instead, which converts
to no key at all, so stores with a sequence key path refused every value with a DataError and
indexes with one got no records. Make an Array.

Validation: Host WPT tests/wpt/tests/IndexedDB (4,511 subtests), 8 processes, on top of the previous commit: SpiderMonkey 3,369 (previous commit 3,298, P2 tip 3,289), QuickJS 3,371 (P2 tip 3,290); the 75 new passes in both are keypath.any.js (7 sequence key path subtests) and key_valid.any.js (18, which store under a ['x', 'keypath'] key path) in window, worker and sharedworker, and the previous commit's binary still fails them; the other differences are whole-test timeouts that pass 5 of 5 alone on both engines: SpiderMonkey get-databases.any.worker, idbfactory-origin-isolation and transaction-abort-multiple-metadata-revert.any.worker, QuickJS idbdatabase-createObjectStore-exception-order.any.sharedworker and idbindex-rename-abort.any.sharedworker. Expectations updated with `./mach update-wpt` from both engines' runs. /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ 134 of 134 on both engines and with --multiprocess. A page probe read back from the SQLite file gives ['a', 'b'] index records of [1, "x"] where the previous commit stored none. At this commit, DAYU200 (QuickJS + RDB, 2 processes): WPT IndexedDB/ 3,367 (P2 tip 3,281), the same 84 new passes as the host plus two flips that pass, nothing newly failing, the unexpected timeouts the known board set (interleaved-cursors-large, idbfactory-origin-isolation, rename and metadata-revert worker/sharedworker variants); /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ 134 of 134; `./mach test-unit --ohos -p servo-storage` RDB only 123 passed, 3 skipped (P2 tip 116), SQLite and RDB 215 passed, 4 skipped (201). `RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings" ./mach build --use-crown --locked --profile checked-release` passes. These counts predate the P3 review fixes folded into the previous commit, which add the fork test index-keys-page-code.any.js (2 subtests in 4 globals).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; found the plain object with a probe of the stored index records, fixed it and ran the WPT runs)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 components/script/dom/indexeddb/key.rs        |   6 +-
 tests/wpt/meta/IndexedDB/key_valid.any.js.ini | 161 ------------------
 tests/wpt/meta/IndexedDB/keypath.any.js.ini   |  63 -------
 3 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 225 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/script/dom/indexeddb/key.rs b/components/script/dom/indexeddb/key.rs
index ce3910682b2..e97cb59ff7e 100644
--- a/components/script/dom/indexeddb/key.rs
+++ b/components/script/dom/indexeddb/key.rs
@@ -653,7 +653,11 @@ pub(crate) fn evaluate_key_path_on_value(
         // Step 1. If keyPath is a list of strings, then:
         KeyPath::StringSequence(key_path) => {
             // Step 1.1. Let result be a new Array object created as if by the expression [].
-            rooted!(&in(cx) let mut result = JS_NewObject(cx, None));
+            // SAFETY: `cx` is a live context; the new array is rooted right away.
+            rooted!(&in(cx) let mut result = unsafe { NewArrayObject1(cx.raw_cx(), 0) });
+            if result.is_null() {
+                return Err(Error::JSFailed);
+            }
 
             // Step 1.2. Let i be 0.
             // Step 1.3. For each item in keyPath:
